### Android — Kotlin + Compose

| Topic | Guidance |
|-------|-----------|
| **HTTP stack** | **OkHttp** `WebSocketListener` — same process as the rest of the app; use a long-lived **`OkHttpClient`** (singleton or DI). |
| **Where to own the socket** | A **`ViewModel`** scoped to the app (`Application` + `viewModelScope`) or a small **singleton `NoolvaAgentConnection`**. Avoid tying the socket only to a single screen if alarms should survive navigation. |
| **Compose** | Expose alarms with **`StateFlow<AlarmEvent?>`** or **`SharedFlow`**; collect in root composable with **`collectAsState()`** / **`collectLatest`**, or show **`Snackbar`**, **dialog**, or route to a dedicated alarms screen. |
| **Threading** | In **`onMessage`**, **`Handler(Looper.getMainLooper()).post { … }`**, **`runOnUiThread`**, or **`withContext(Dispatchers.Main)`** before mutating UI state. |
| **Persistent alarm UX** | **`NotificationManager`** (+ channel) with **`alarm_id`** in extras; optionally a **foreground service** if you must hold the socket in background (battery / policy tradeoffs). |
| **Lifecycle** | **`ProcessLifecycleOwner`** or **`LifecycleService`**: reconnect when app returns to foreground; pause or teardown if you do not need background alarms. |
| **Token** | **EncryptedSharedPreferences** or **DataStore** for PAT; build URL or `Authorization: Bearer` on **`Request.Builder`**. |
| **Cleartext** | **`ws://`** on device/emulator may need **`networkSecurityConfig`** (dev only). Ship **`wss://`** in production. |

**OkHttp + alarm branch (outline):**

```kotlin
// java.net.URLEncoder for query token
val wsUrl = "$baseWss/api/ws/$deviceId?token=${URLEncoder.encode(pat, Charsets.UTF_8.name())}"
val client = OkHttpClient.Builder()
  .pingInterval(0, TimeUnit.SECONDS)
  .build()
client.newWebSocket(Request.Builder().url(wsUrl).build(), object : WebSocketListener() {
  override fun onMessage(webSocket: WebSocket, text: String) {
    val o = JSONObject(text)
    when (o.optString("type")) {
      "alarm" -> {
        val id = o.optString("alarm_id")
        val payload = o.optJSONObject("payload")
        scope.launch(Dispatchers.Main) {
          alarmEvents.tryEmit(AlarmEvent(id, payload))
        }
      }
    }
  }
  override fun onFailure(ws: WebSocket, t: Throwable, response: Response?) { /* schedule reconnect */ }
})
// kotlinx.coroutines fixed-periodic: webSocket.send("""{"type":"ping"}""")
```

