### iOS — SwiftUI

| Topic | Guidance |
|-------|-----------|
| **API** | **`URLSessionWebSocketTask`** (iOS 13+) — create with **`URLSession.shared.webSocketTask(with: URL)`** where the URL includes **`/api/ws/<device_id>?token=...`**. |
| **Receive loop** | Call **`receive(completionHandler:)`**; on success with **`.string(text)`**, parse **`Data(text.utf8)`** with **`JSONDecoder`** or **`JSONSerialization`**; then call **`receive` again** to keep the loop going. |
| **Send ping** | **`task.send(.string("{\"type\":\"ping\"}"))`** with a **`Timer`** or **`Task` + sleep** on an interval. |
| **SwiftUI** | Hold the task in an **`ObservableObject`** / **`@StateObject`**; publish `@Published var lastAlarm: AlarmPush?` on **`DispatchQueue.main.async`**. Views react with **`onChange`**, sheets, or banners. |
| **Background** | Prefer **`wss://`**. For notifications when the app is not active, request **`UNUserNotificationCenter`** permission and post a local notification when **`type == "alarm"`**. |
| **Reconnect** | On receive/delegate failure, **`cancel()`** the task and open a new one; exponential backoff. |

**Receive loop (outline):**

```swift
func receiveLoop(_ task: URLSessionWebSocketTask) {
  task.receive { result in
    defer { receiveLoop(task) }
    guard case .success(let message) = result,
          case .string(let text) = message,
          let data = text.data(using: .utf8),
          let obj = try? JSONSerialization.jsonObject(with: data) as? [String: Any],
          obj["type"] as? String == "alarm" else { return }
    let alarmId = obj["alarm_id"] as? String ?? ""
    DispatchQueue.main.async { /* @Published / UNUserNotification */ }
  }
}
task.resume()
receiveLoop(task)
```

