### Windows — C# + WinUI 3

| Topic | Guidance |
|-------|-----------|
| **Client** | **`System.Net.WebSockets.ClientWebSocket`** (or **`Windows.Networking.Sockets.MessageWebSocket`**; below assumes **`ClientWebSocket`** for portability). |
| **Connect** | `var ws = new ClientWebSocket();` optionally **`ws.Options.SetRequestHeader("Authorization", $"Bearer {pat}")`** if you omit query token; then **`await ws.ConnectAsync(uri, CancellationToken)`** with `Uri` including **`/api/ws/{deviceId}?token=...`**. |
| **Receive** | Loop **`await ws.ReceiveAsync(buffer, ct)`**, decode UTF-8 to string, **`JsonDocument.Parse`**, check **`RootElement.GetProperty("type")`**. |
| **UI thread** | **`DispatcherQueue.GetForCurrentThread().TryEnqueue(() => { ... })`** (or the Window’s dispatcher) before touching XAML state or showing **`ContentDialog`**. |
| **Alarm UI** | In-app: **`InfoBar`**, dialog, or toast via **`AppNotificationManager`** (Windows App SDK) for user-visible alerts. |
| **Ping** | **`PeriodicTimer`** or **`Task.Delay` loop** sending UTF-8 bytes of `{"type":"ping"}`. |
| **Reconnect** | Catch **`WebSocketException`**, dispose socket, backoff, **`ConnectAsync`** again. |

